      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the review and the `UseCompactObjectHeaders` suggestion.\n\nDone in both layers:\n\n- Bazel build server + tests (change 638023): host_jvm_args for the server JVM, --jvmopt for test JVMs.\n- Gerrit runtime, default-on via site init (change 638024): a small InitJdkOptions step writes -XX:+UseCompactObjectHeaders to container.javaOptions, so new sites get it and existing sites pick it up on their next init/upgrade.\n\nWe\u0027re on Bazel 9.2.0, so the flags are passed manually; on Bazel 10.x the `--experimental_use_compact_object_headers` startup option is default-on, and on JDK 27 compact object headers are the JVM default, so the explicit flags can be dropped then.",
